# Story / narrative authoring

**POV authority:** [narrative-pov.md](../../docs/02-systems/narrative-pov.md) · **Scenes:** [story-events README](../../docs/03-content/story-events/README.md)

## Scope

- Edit **design-docs** story drafts (`textKey` / `textEn`), guided-tutorial copy, and narrative sections in linked system docs.
- **Do not** change `griddungeon-game` C#, Unity assets, or combat/campaign **rules** unless the user explicitly asks to document a new beat for engineering.

## Navigator (locked)

- Player **is** the active Navigator: **Act 1 solo** in the labyrinth; after hub recruitment, walks **sideline** with the six-core party (off formation). Guides via **kit / map sense** (low myth) — not a grid fighter, not a core class voice.
- **Avoid** comms / channel / line / radio diction in S1 scripts unless explicitly requested.
- **Blank state** at new game ([narrative-pov](../../docs/02-systems/narrative-pov.md)); no Synchro/Protocol vocabulary until the unlock beat teaches it.
- **First person** on **Navigator** story-VN steps only; other characters use **`npc:*`** (or `narrator`) when the scene needs dialogue **with** the Navigator — never **`core:<id>`**. **Guided tutorials** = impersonal coach (no character speaker).

## Handoff to implementation

When copy is final, tell the user to sync `Assets/Content/StoryEvents/` in the game repo — do not invent test results or run Unity from this rule.
